          "content": {
            "id": "884031db-4bbb-3a6e-b36e-e227f74dd513",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Oracle slides on AI overpromise, says market expert",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Shares of Oracle fell nearly 5% after a report said the cloud company's largest data center partner Blue Owl Capital will not back a $10 billion deal for its next AI data center facility.</p><p>Coons said the pullback also reflects a normal repricing process rather than signs of a broader AI bubble.</p><p>\"I think this is really healthy for all those that talk about a AI bubble, I think this proves that there isn't one because this is so much different than the dotcom bubble, because there are healthy discussions and healthy pullbacks like this for certain names that probably deserve it,\" he said.</p></body></title>",
